          "command": "cat >> /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-7-report.md << 'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## Follow-up: Reviewer Finding Fix — deadline_s not a shared budget across drain\n\n### Finding\n\n`Shipper.drain(spool, deadline_s)` passed the same full `deadline_s` to\n`_ship_with_retry()` for every pending segment, so a multi-segment drain\nwith N retryable-then-ok segments could take up to `N x deadline_s` instead\nof being bounded by `deadline_s` as a whole. This contradicted the\n`EventClient.flush(timeout_s)` contract in `docs/modules/event-messaging.md`,\nwhich frames the deadline as bounding the entire drain call.\n\n### Fix\n\n`drain()` now records `start = time.monotonic()` once at the top, and for\neach pending segment (when `deadline_s` is not `None`) computes\n`remaining_budget = deadline_s - (time.monotonic() - start)`. If\n`remaining_budget <= 0` the loop breaks immediately (spool holds, next flush\nretries — same handling as a RETRYABLE outcome); otherwise `remaining_budget`\n(not the original `deadline_s`) is passed to `_ship_with_retry`. The\nno-deadline (`deadline_s is None`) path is unchanged. Added `import time` to\n`src/common/msging/shipper.py`.\n\n### TDD Evidence\n\n**RED** — added `test_drain_deadline_bounds_whole_drain` to\n`tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py`: two sealed spool segments; a\ntransport whose first call sleeps 0.25s then ACKs (segment 1), and always\nreturns 503 thereafter (segment 2, always retryable). With `deadline_s=0.3`:\n\n```\n$ ./venv/bin/pytest tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py::test_drain_deadline_bounds_whole_drain -v\nFAILED tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py::test_drain_deadline_bounds_whole_drain\nassert 0.5873708329163492 < 0.45\n```\n\n(Note: an earlier draft of this test used \"both segments always return 503\"\nper the initial finding wording, but that scenario doesn't actually\ndistinguish buggy vs. fixed code — `drain()` already `break`s on the first\nRETRYABLE outcome, so only one segment is ever attempted regardless of the\nbudget bug. The redesigned test above makes segment 1 succeed after\nconsuming real wall-clock time so the loop proceeds to segment 2, which is\nwhere the shared-vs-per-segment budget difference becomes observable.)\n\n**GREEN** — after the fix:\n\n```\n$ ./venv/bin/pytest tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py -v\n11 passed in 0.51s\n```\n\n**Full suite**:\n\n```\n$ ./venv/bin/pytest tests/common/msging -v\n43 passed in 0.53s\n```\n\n### Files Changed\n\n- `src/common/msging/shipper.py` — `drain()` budget fix, `import time` added.\n- `tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py` — new\n  `test_drain_deadline_bounds_whole_drain` test, `import time` added.\n\n### Commit\n\n```\n4d02997 fix(msging): drain deadline is a total budget across segments\n2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n```\n\nBranch: `feature/event-msging`.\nEOF\necho done"
