        "text": "You are fixing one reviewer finding in `src/common/msging/shipper.py` in the repo /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ. Work from that directory.\n\n## Finding: deadline_s is not a shared budget across a multi-segment drain\n`Shipper.drain(spool, deadline_s)` loops over `spool.pending()` and calls `self._ship_with_retry(envelopes, deadline_s)` with the SAME full deadline for every segment. With N retryable-then-ok segments, drain() can take up to N × deadline_s. The contract (docs/modules/event-messaging.md, EventClient.flush(timeout_s)) frames the deadline as bounding the WHOLE drain call.\n\n**Fix:** make deadline_s a total budget for the drain. At drain start record `start = time.monotonic()`; for each segment compute `remaining_budget = deadline_s - (time.monotonic() - start)`; if remaining_budget <= 0, stop the loop (treat like RETRYABLE: spool holds, next flush retries); otherwise pass `remaining_budget` to `_ship_with_retry`. The no-deadline path (deadline_s is None) is unchanged.\n\n## Your job (TDD)\n1. Add one failing test to `tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py` (follow existing style/helpers there):\n   - `test_drain_deadline_bounds_whole_drain`: config with retry_backoff base 0.01/max 0.02; spool with TWO sealed segments (append then seal() twice); a transport that always returns 503; call `drain(spool, deadline_s=0.3)` and wrap it with time measurement — assert the total elapsed time is < 1.0 s (comfortably under 2×deadline+slack while proving it didn't run 2 full budgets serially... actually with always-503 both segments would each burn a full 0.3s budget in the buggy version = ~0.6s+, fixed version = ~0.3s total; assert elapsed < 0.5 and result.shipped == 0 and remaining == 2).\n2. Run it, confirm it fails against current code: `./venv/bin/pytest tests/common/msging/test_shipper.py -v`\n3. Apply the minimal fix to `Shipper.drain` as described.\n4. Run the covering test file, then the full suite once: `./venv/bin/pytest tests/common/msging -v` — all must pass.\n5. Commit as one commit with message: `fix(msging): drain deadline is a total budget across segments`\n   (Never mention Claude/AI; no Co-Authored-By lines.)\n6. Append a fix report to /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-7-report.md: what changed, covering tests, commands run, output summary.\n\nReport back with ONLY (under 10 lines): status, commit SHA + subject, test summary (command + counts), report file path.",
